{"parentUuid":"886e138c-9137-438b-970a-6a92a8863d9c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Act4YHWQiY5r7PdPQAEtmw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SAT competition 2025 GPU track parallel solvers results\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33211/35366\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=uUsL07BsMA\"},{\"title\":\"Gradient-Guided Boolean Satisfiability Accelerated on ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397521398_TurboSAT_Gradient-Guided_Boolean_Satisfiability_Accelerated_on_GPU-CPU_Hybrid_System/fulltext/6913fc3aa2b691617b6b1e04/TurboSAT-Gradient-Guided-Boolean-Satisfiability-Accelerated-on-GPU-CPU-Hybrid-System.pdf?origin=scientificContributions\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlining Distributed SAT Solver Design Dominik Schreiber # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/SchreiberRigiLupertiBiere-SAT25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - satcompetition/2025: SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/satcompetition/2025\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - JerrySWE/CPU-GPU-Parallel-SAT-Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JerrySWE/CPU-GPU-Parallel-SAT-Solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about SAT Competition 2025. The competition uses a PAR-2 ranking scheme that favors solvers that are faster, not only those that count solved instances.\n\nRegarding the parallel track specifically, the parallel track timeout was reduced to 1000 seconds (previously 5000 seconds). The first search result appears to be a presentation about the SAT Competition 2025 results.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific detailed results for the GPU track and parallel solvers in SAT Competition 2025. The PDF from the official SAT Competition 2025 results presentation was found, but the extracted content primarily covers administrative changes, memory issues, and output standardization rather than specific GPU track results.\n\nFor more detailed information about the specific winners and performance metrics of GPU track solvers, you would need to visit the official SAT Competition 2025 website directly or download the full results presentation from their repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"21241fe6-6a9b-494e-aef3-a4f3eb3f6c65","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:52.365Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"886e138c-9137-438b-970a-6a92a8863d9c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ff33e095-5d8f-4a67-a4d4-4e9209abbc76","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qx6gB5p3vvpyb96tcL8HDT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ParaFROST GPU SAT solver 2025 2026 latest version benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - muhos/ParaFROST: A Parallel SAT Solver with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/muhos/ParaFROST\"},{\"title\":\"Large SAT Benchmark Suite for Certified SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/5138008\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://gears.win.tue.nl/papers/parafrost_gpu.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33211/35366\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU-Accelerated Inprocessing – GEARS: An NWO TOP funded research project\",\"url\":\"https://gears.win.tue.nl/software/parafrost/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/372857962_Certified_SAT_solving_with_GPU_accelerated_inprocessing\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72016-2_8\"},{\"title\":\"Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing | Formal Methods in System Design | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10703-023-00432-z\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing Muhammad Osama (\\u0000)1 ∗\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1304678997/34\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7979176/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ParaFROST GPU SAT solver:\n\n## Overview\n\nParaFROST is a parallel SAT solver with GPU-accelerated inprocessing capable of harnessing NVIDIA CUDA-enabled GPUs in applying modern simplification techniques in parallel. The CDCL search is built from scratch with various optimisations based on CaDiCaL heuristics.\n\n## Key Technical Features\n\nThe work introduces the first attempt to parallelize inprocessing on GPU architectures, with new space-efficient data structures and a data-parallel garbage collector that runs in parallel on the GPU to reduce memory consumption and improve memory access locality, with the parallel variable elimination algorithm being twice as fast as previous work.\n\nIn latest work, the data structure used in ParaFROST has been compacted to allow effective solving optimisations, and a memory-aware Bounded Variable Elimination (BVE) was introduced to avoid running out of memory due to adding too many new clauses.\n\n## Benchmark Performance\n\nIn experiments, ParaFROST solves numerous benchmarks faster on the GPU than its sequential counterparts. PFROST-GPU dominates over PFROST-CPU and CaDiCaL, and seems more effective on UNSAT formulas than CaDiCaL.\n\n## Recent Development\n\nThe most recent published work on ParaFROST appears to be from 2024, focusing on certified SAT solving with GPU-accelerated inprocessing and proof generation capabilities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"91474fe2-19f6-4aff-8530-726812b8a6c3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:52.861Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ff33e095-5d8f-4a67-a4d4-4e9209abbc76","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2975cd2e-ee31-4c6a-99b0-5e3aa474a88c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R3TbX5GJfGJZ7m15EuJuaJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FPGA SAT solver 2025 commercial product accelerator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA | Proceedings of the 2025 ACM/SIGDA International Symposium on Field Programmable Gate Arrays\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3706628.3708869\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3706628.3708869\"},{\"title\":\"Hardware-Accelerated SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://carleton.scholaris.ca/items/4a37578d-6f34-4b3b-8c7e-c40539c4ea59\"},{\"title\":\"An Efficient Hardware Implementation of a SAT Problem Solver on FPGA | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/6628279/\"},{\"title\":\"FPGAs (Can Get Some) SATisfaction\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.11279v1\"},{\"title\":\"FPGA-Based SAT Solver | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/4054862/\"},{\"title\":\"An Approach for Solving Large SAT Problems on FPGA | ACM Transactions on Reconfigurable Technology and Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/1857927.1857937\"},{\"title\":\"Reconfigurable hardware accelerator for boolean satisfiability solver - Microsoft Corporation\",\"url\":\"https://www.freepatentsonline.com/8131660.html\"},{\"title\":\"FPGA Acceleration of a Stochastic Local Search Portfolio Solver for Boolean Satisfiability | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9859479/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) FPGA based accelerator for 3-SAT conflict analysis in SAT solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221104770_FPGA_based_accelerator_for_3-SAT_conflict_analysis_in_SAT_solvers\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about FPGA SAT solver commercial products and accelerators in 2025:\n\n## Recent Key Development\n\nSAT-Accel is an algorithm-hardware co-design solver that applies many of the core improvements found in modern SAT solvers. This was presented at the 2025 ACM/SIGDA International Symposium on Field Programmable Gate Arrays (FPGA '25) in February-March 2025 in Monterey, CA.\n\nAlthough improvements in SAT solving have found their way onto CPU implementations, there has been limited progress adopting this on hardware accelerators mainly because it is difficult to implement the dynamic data structures needed to support a modern SAT solving algorithm. SAT-Accel uses a novel memory management system and representation that supports the dynamic data structures required by a modern SAT solving algorithm.\n\n## Other Notable Recent Work\n\nIn 2024, FYalSAT was developed as a high-throughput stochastic local search K-SAT solver on FPGA, and research has explored multi-threading and global accessing techniques using the Xilinx Alveo U280 accelerator card for FPGA-based SAT solvers.\n\nThe research landscape shows that while FPGA acceleration of SAT solvers has been an active area of study for years, SAT-Accel represents a notable 2025 advancement in bringing modern SAT solving techniques to FPGA hardware.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cf86a396-73b9-4a95-bfde-b07cbb20a81f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:54.930Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2975cd2e-ee31-4c6a-99b0-5e3aa474a88c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"04b91047-b256-4dd0-8f9d-64cb329041ff","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012eLQf97DUUoQf2xfeSZfne","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"D-Wave Advantage2 quantum annealing 2025 placement packing benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Performance gains in the D-Wave Advantage2 system at the 4,400-qubit scale\",\"url\":\"https://www.dwavequantum.com/media/wakjcpsf/adv2_4400q_whitepaper-1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"D-Wave Deep Dive: A Look at The Quantum Advantage Findings -- And The Questions That Remain\",\"url\":\"https://thequantuminsider.com/2025/03/13/d-wave-deep-dive-a-look-at-the-quantum-advantage-findings-and-the-questions-that-remain/\"},{\"title\":\"Quantum annealing applications, challenges and limitations for optimisation problems compared to classical solvers | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-96220-2\"},{\"title\":\"D-Wave Claims Quantum Supremacy with Quantum Annealing\",\"url\":\"https://postquantum.com/industry-news/d-wave-quantum-advantage/\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond-classical computation in quantum simulation | Science\",\"url\":\"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.ado6285\"},{\"title\":\"Resources\",\"url\":\"https://www.dwavequantum.com/resources/\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmarking Advantage and D-Wave 2000Q quantum annealers with exact cover problems | Quantum Information Processing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11128-022-03476-y\"},{\"title\":\"Comparing Quantum Annealing and BF-DCQO\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.14358v1\"},{\"title\":\"Quantum Annealing In 2025: Achieving Quantum Supremacy, Practical Applications And Industrial Adoption - Brian D. Colwell\",\"url\":\"https://briandcolwell.com/quantum-annealing-in-2025-achieving-quantum-supremacy-practical-applications-and-industrial-adoption/\"},{\"title\":\"Annealing quantum computing’s long-term future\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d42473-025-00236-1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about D-Wave Advantage2's quantum annealing benchmarks, though the results focus more on simulation problems rather than explicit \"placement packing\" benchmarks. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key 2025 Benchmarks for D-Wave Advantage2\n\nIn a peer-reviewed study published in Science on March 12, 2025, D-Wave's researchers report that their 5,000+ qubit Advantage2 prototype quantum annealer outperformed one of the world's most powerful supercomputers (Oak Ridge National Lab's Frontier system) in simulating the quantum dynamics of a complex magnetic material.\n\nD-Wave benchmarked the performance of the Advantage2 quantum-processing unit (QPU), a 4,400+ annealing quantum computer interconnected in the Zephyr topology, against a previous-generation QPU on the optimization task of solving 3D-lattice spin glasses of tunable precision.\n\nIn some cases, the Advantage2 system produces better quality solutions using anneal times that are several orders of magnitude faster than those used on the previous-generation Advantage system.\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\nThe connectivity between qubits in the new processor is higher (Advantage2 uses D-Wave's Pegasus topology where each qubit can connect to 15 others), and higher connectivity meant the 3D lattice of the spin glass could be embedded more naturally onto the hardware graph, with fewer extra qubits needed to mediate long-range connections.\n\nThe search results primarily document benchmarks for quantum dynamics simulations and optimization tasks rather than specific \"placement packing\" problem benchmarks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2840c64f-4f95-4469-98dc-51d0c6beab45","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:55.315Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"04b91047-b256-4dd0-8f9d-64cb329041ff","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0d9ae612-2bf0-4342-8381-d654f03d76a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017bzD8bZVEveFqmFzCJwrQ9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NVIDIA cuOpt GPU MIP LP solver 2026 benchmark OR-Tools comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cuOpt | Decision Optimization | NVIDIA\",\"url\":\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - NVIDIA/cuopt: GPU accelerated decision optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt\"},{\"title\":\"cuGenOpt: A GPU-Accelerated General-Purpose Metaheuristic Framework for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.19163\"},{\"title\":\"Rose cuOpt - SimpleRose\",\"url\":\"https://simplerose.com/rosecuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Optimization with GAMS and NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2025/09/gpu-accelerated-optimization-with-gams-and-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Learn How NVIDIA cuOpt Accelerates Mixed Integer Optimization using Primal Heuristics | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/learn-how-nvidia-cuopt-accelerates-mixed-integer-optimization-using-primal-heuristics\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Large Linear Programming Problems with NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-large-linear-programming-problems-with-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerate Decision Optimization Using Open Source NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerate-decision-optimization-using-open-source-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA cuOpt Solver Cracks Four Previously Unsolved Optimization Problems\",\"url\":\"https://bitcoinethereumnews.com/tech/nvidia-cuopt-solver-cracks-four-previously-unsolved-optimization-problems/\"},{\"title\":\"First-order methods in Linear Programming: PDHG and GPU-friendly LP solvers | Ebrahim Pichka\",\"url\":\"https://epichka.com/blog/2026/fom-lp/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding NVIDIA cuOpt GPU MIP/LP solver and comparisons with OR-Tools:\n\n## NVIDIA cuOpt Overview\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt is an open source, GPU-accelerated engine for decision optimization, excelling in mixed-integer programming (MIP), linear programming (LP), vehicle routing problems (VRPs), and quadratic programming (QP). It enables near real-time solutions for large-scale LPs with millions of variables and constraints, and MIPs with hundreds of thousands of variables.\n\n## Performance Benchmarks\n\ncuOpt solves LP, MIP, and VRP problems 10x to 5,000x faster with GPU acceleration. More specifically for LP problems, the NVIDIA cuOpt LP solver achieves over 5,000x faster performance compared to CPU-based solvers by leveraging the Primal-Dual Linear Programming (PDLP) algorithm and NVIDIA GPU acceleration.\n\nFor MIP problems, NVIDIA's GPU-accelerated cuOpt engine discovers new solutions for four MIPLIB benchmark problems, outperforming CPU solvers with 22% lower objective gaps.\n\n## Comparison with OR-Tools\n\nGoogle OR-Tools provides MIP solver interfaces and a specialized Routing solver based on Guided Local Search (GLS), achieving strong performance on TSP/VRP but unable to express custom semantics such as intra-route priority constraints. Google made PDLP available in OR-Tools for large-scale applications.\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt is a commercial-grade GPU-accelerated solver covering MILP/LP and vehicle routing, achieving state-of-the-art performance on standard benchmarks. However, its problem scope is fixed: the routing module supports only predefined VRP constraint types, the MILP module requires explicit linear formulations, and users cannot define arbitrary black-box objectives.\n\n## Recent Updates (2026)\n\nIn April 2026, the GAMS/cuOpt solver link was extended for NVIDIA cuOpt 26.04 which added the pdlp_precision option, and new and updated options for MIP, especially options to fine tune heuristics.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"de2aaaea-1b39-499d-9df1-8eacc65bb09d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:55.883Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d9ae612-2bf0-4342-8381-d654f03d76a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
