{"parentUuid":"e3fd1a2f-f162-42b9-9958-4399e22f5b42","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XHccFJ3qY7MFcbXBSUFigU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LGx2gpA1wpK5jTDBmLTSJq","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/muhos/ParaFROST","prompt":"What is the latest release version, release date, and what changes from 2024-2026? Does it do end-to-end CDCL on GPU or only inprocessing?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11360,"cache_read_input_tokens":24608,"output_tokens":459,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11360},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":24608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11360,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosTuHUS5SJcTnksqrmW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"530a4e4b-ae81-4db4-a8db-876a35cf079d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:17.269Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b3085297-c763-4bc4-aa51-3d570178038a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qw1XszpqPrP2N2qGDfpvNC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"TurboSAT\" GPU CPU hybrid SAT solver 2025 paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2511.07737] TurboSAT: Gradient-Guided Boolean Satisfiability Accelerated on GPU-CPU Hybrid System\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.07737\"},{\"title\":\"Turbosat: GPU-CPU Hybrid System Achieves 200x Acceleration Of Boolean Satisfiability With Gradient-Guided Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://quantumzeitgeist.com/200x-optimization-turbosat-gpu-cpu-hybrid-system-achieves-acceleration-boolean-satisfiability/\"},{\"title\":\"TurboSAT: Gradient-Guided Boolean Satisfiability Accelerated on GPU-CPU Hybrid System\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.07737v1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) TurboSAT: Gradient-Guided Boolean Satisfiability Accelerated on GPU-CPU Hybrid System\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397521398_TurboSAT_Gradient-Guided_Boolean_Satisfiability_Accelerated_on_GPU-CPU_Hybrid_System\"},{\"title\":\"TurboSAT: Gradient-Guided Boolean Satisfiability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.07737\"},{\"title\":\"On the Unreasonable Effectiveness of SAT Solvers | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347888380_On_the_Unreasonable_Effectiveness_of_SAT_Solvers\"},{\"title\":\"Restart strategies | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Restart-strategies_fig1_220163323\"},{\"title\":\"Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33211/35366\"},{\"title\":\"FourierSAT: A Fourier Expansion-Based Algebraic Framework for Solving Hybrid Boolean Constraints | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/342537926_FourierSAT_A_Fourier_Expansion-Based_Algebraic_Framework_for_Solving_Hybrid_Boolean_Constraints\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://gears.win.tue.nl/papers/parafrost_gpu.pdf\"}]\n\nI found the paper you're looking for! Here's what I found about TurboSAT:\n\n## Overview\n\nTurboSAT is titled \"Gradient-Guided Boolean Satisfiability Accelerated on GPU-CPU Hybrid System\" and was published in November 2025.\n\n## Key Technical Approach\n\nThe research formulates the SAT problem as a binarized matrix-matrix multiplication layer that could be optimized using a differentiable objective function, combining the strengths of parallel differentiable optimization and sequential search to accelerate SAT on a hybrid GPU-CPU system.\n\n## System Architecture\n\nThe hybrid solver has two complementary components:\n\n1. GPUs leverage parallel differentiable solving to rapidly evaluate SAT clauses and use gradients to stochastically explore the solution space and optimize variable assignments.\n\n2. Promising partial assignments generated by the GPUs are post-processed on many CPU threads which exploit conflict-driven sequential search to further traverse the solution subspaces and identify complete assignments.\n\n## Performance Results\n\nPrototyping the hybrid solver on an NVIDIA DGX GB200 node, the solver achieves runtime speedups up to over 200x when compared to a state-of-the-art CPU-based solver on public satisfiable benchmark problems from the SAT Competition.\n\nThe paper is available on arXiv at https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.07737.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"70c0a5a8-03e4-4988-9646-82655ce06e6f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:19.673Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b3085297-c763-4bc4-aa51-3d570178038a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e3fd1a2f-f162-42b9-9958-4399e22f5b42","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dow9rvbpKmBuai2ccHreLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"SAT-Accel\" FPGA Alveo SAT solver speedup 2025 ASPLOS\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA | Proceedings of the 2025 ACM/SIGDA International Symposium on Field Programmable Gate Arrays\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3706628.3708869\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3706628.3708869\"},{\"title\":\"PackSAT: An FPGA-accelerated Circuit SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://etd.ohiolink.edu/acprod/odb_etd/ws/send_file/send?accession=ucin1692282072060783&disposition=inline\"},{\"title\":\"FPGA Acceleration of a Stochastic Local Search Portfolio Solver for Boolean Satisfiability | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9859479/\"},{\"title\":\"FPGAs (Can Get Some) SATisfaction\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.11279v1\"},{\"title\":\"Hardware-Accelerated SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://carleton.scholaris.ca/items/4a37578d-6f34-4b3b-8c7e-c40539c4ea59\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-Accel: A Modern SAT Solver on a FPGA | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/389394986_SAT-Accel_A_Modern_SAT_Solver_on_a_FPGA\"},{\"title\":\"FPGA-based SAT solver architecture with near-zero synthesis and layout overhead | IEE Proceedings - Computers and Digital Techniques\",\"url\":\"https://digital-library.theiet.org/doi/abs/10.1049/ip-cdt:20000482\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Boolean Constraint Propagation for Efficient SAT-Solving on FPGAs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2401.07429v2\"},{\"title\":\"An Efficient Hardware Implementation of a SAT Problem Solver on FPGA | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/6628279/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about SAT-Accel:\n\n## Overview\n\nSAT-Accel is an algorithm-hardware co-design solver that applies many of the core improvements found in modern SAT solvers. SAT-Accel uses a novel memory management system and representation that supports the dynamic data structures required by a modern SAT solving algorithm.\n\n## Performance\n\nCompared to the current state-of-the-art stand-alone hardware accelerator, SAT-Hard, SAT-Accel achieves on average 800.0x speedup.\n\n## Publication\n\nSAT-Accel was presented at the 2025 ACM/SIGDA International Symposium on Field Programmable Gate Arrays (FPGA '25). This publication covers a modern SAT solver implementation on FPGA hardware.\n\n## Key Innovation\n\nThe work addresses a significant challenge in FPGA-based SAT acceleration: although improvements have been found in CPU implementations, there has been limited progress adopting this on hardware accelerators mainly because it is difficult to implement the dynamic data structures needed to support a modern SAT solving algorithm. SAT-Accel overcomes this limitation through its novel approach to memory management and data structure support.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f8a6f945-bb33-415a-80ec-271c6177230c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:21.824Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3fd1a2f-f162-42b9-9958-4399e22f5b42","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"530a4e4b-ae81-4db4-a8db-876a35cf079d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LGx2gpA1wpK5jTDBmLTSJq","type":"tool_result","content":"# ParaFROST Release Information\n\n**Latest Release:** ParaFROST 3.5.0 (April 10, 2026)\n\nThe webpage doesn't provide specific details about what changed between 2024-2026, only listing that 29 releases exist total.\n\n**GPU Execution Scope:**\n\nParaFROST performs GPU-accelerated inprocessing specifically. The solver description states: \"The CDCL search is built from scratch with various optimisations based on CaDiCaL heuristics.\" This indicates the core CDCL search algorithm runs on CPU, while \"The inprocessing engine extends our previous work in SIGmA simplifier with new data structures, parallel garbage collection\" leveraging GPU acceleration. \n\nSo to directly answer your question: ParaFROST handles inprocessing on GPU, not end-to-end CDCL."}]},"uuid":"ce73d724-660d-430c-a1da-8c35daaba4b0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:22.207Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"530a4e4b-ae81-4db4-a8db-876a35cf079d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"95d19e3b-26bc-4344-9399-8c620576f42b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SS5oKRME3bUe2ddYaey6Xc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cuOpt MIP MIPLIB benchmark 2026 vs Gurobi CPU consumer GPU\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Does Gurobi support GPUs? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360012237852-Does-Gurobi-support-GPUs\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA cuOpt Solver Cracks Four Previously Unsolved Optimization Problems\",\"url\":\"https://bitcoinethereumnews.com/tech/nvidia-cuopt-solver-cracks-four-previously-unsolved-optimization-problems/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Optimization with GAMS and NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2025/09/gpu-accelerated-optimization-with-gams-and-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"Boosting Mathematical Optimization Performance and Energy Efficiency on the NVIDIA Grace CPU - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/resources/boosting-mathematical-optimization-performance-and-energy-efficiency-on-the-nvidia-grace-cpu/\"},{\"title\":\"Learn How NVIDIA cuOpt Accelerates Mixed Integer Optimization using Primal Heuristics | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/learn-how-nvidia-cuopt-accelerates-mixed-integer-optimization-using-primal-heuristics\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi 8 Performance Benchmarks February 11, 2019\",\"url\":\"https://assets.gurobi.com/pdfs/benchmarks.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Project Report on MIP Parameter Tuning for Gurobi | willweiao.blog\",\"url\":\"https://willweiao.github.io/posts/a_project_report_on_mip_parameter_tuning_for_gurobi/\"},{\"title\":\"Using GPUs to Solve LPs: What’s in It for Me? - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/resources/using-gpus-to-solve-lps-whats-in-it-for-me/\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started with NVIDIA CuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://atalaykutlay.com/getting-started-with-cuopt.html\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Benchmarks for Current Linear and Mixed Integer Optimization Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/288179452_Benchmarks_for_Current_Linear_and_Mixed_Integer_Optimization_Solvers\"}]\n\nHere are the key findings from the search results about cuOpt MIP MIPLIB benchmarks versus Gurobi across CPU and consumer GPU platforms:\n\n## cuOpt GPU Performance on MIPLIB\n\nNVIDIA cuOpt leverages GPU acceleration to implement advanced primal heuristics, achieving significant speedups and improved solution quality for large-scale MIP instances, including previously unsolved MIPLIB benchmarks. Notably, four newly-solved MIPLIB problems—liu.mps, neos-3355120-tarago.mps, polygonpack4-7.mps, and bts4-cta.mps—serve as proof points for enterprises evaluating whether GPU-accelerated optimization delivers on its promises.\n\nAcross benchmark tests, GPU Extended FP with Fix and Propagate found 220.67 feasible solutions on average versus 188.67 for standard Local-MIP—a 17% improvement, with the objective gap dropping to 0.22 compared to 0.46 for the baseline approach.\n\n## cuOpt Architecture\n\nFor MIP, NVIDIA cuOpt uses a hybrid GPU/CPU method, running primal heuristics on the GPU and improving the dual bound on the CPU.\n\n## Gurobi's CPU Performance\n\nThe Gurobi Optimizer on the NVIDIA Grace CPU achieves significant speedups and energy savings, with Grace Hopper outperforming EPYC on most hard models with an average runtime of about 80 seconds versus 130 seconds for AMD—a 38% improvement, running nearly 23% faster while using 46% less energy.\n\n## GPU Limitations for MIP\n\nIt's important to note that Gurobi's development team notes that GPUs aren't well suited to the needs of an LP/MIP solver, as GPUs don't work well for sparse linear algebra and SIMD computation is not well suited to parallel MIP.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7379032e-d6c0-4beb-b749-fc542163819b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:23.084Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"95d19e3b-26bc-4344-9399-8c620576f42b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3600cab8-0d44-4140-9762-cfce25a4bef9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a6e2f3150e1184d9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHL3kM2u7iuBLTdhyY519F","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"D-Wave hybrid quantum bin packing facility placement benchmark 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"D-Wave Documentation — D-Wave Quantum Computing Products documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.ocean.dwavesys.com/en/stable/examples/hybrid_cqm_binpacking.html\"},{\"title\":\"Hybrid approach for solving real-world bin packing problem instances using quantum annealers | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-39013-9\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Packing: Binary CQM — D-Wave Quantum Computing Products documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.dwavequantum.com/en/latest/industrial_optimization/example_cqm_binpacking.html\"},{\"title\":\"BASF and D-Wave Announce Completion of Proof-of-Concept Project, Demonstrating Benchmark in Manufacturing Efficiency\",\"url\":\"https://www.dwavequantum.com/company/newsroom/press-release/basf-and-d-wave-announce-completion-of-proof-of-concept-project-demonstrating-benchmark-in-manufacturing-efficiency/\"},{\"title\":\"Testing quantum and simulated annealers on the drone delivery packing problem | Quantum Machine Intelligence | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s42484-026-00362-z\"},{\"title\":\"BASF and D-Wave Announce PoC with Manufacturing Benchmark | Inside HPC & AI News\",\"url\":\"https://insidehpc.com/2025/11/basf-and-d-wave-announce-poc-with-manufacturing-benchmark/\"},{\"title\":\"Quantum annealing applications, challenges and limitations for optimisation problems compared to classical solvers | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-96220-2\"},{\"title\":\"Comparative Benchmark of a Quantum Algorithm for the Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2207.07460\"},{\"title\":\"Comparative Benchmark of a Quantum Algorithm for the Bin Packing Problem | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10022156/\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation of Quantum and Hybrid Solvers for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.10455\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about D-Wave's hybrid quantum approaches to bin packing and facility optimization. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## D-Wave Hybrid Quantum Bin Packing and Facility Optimization\n\nD-Wave's Q4RealBPP (Quantum for Real Bin Packing Problem) is a hybrid quantum-classical computing framework for real-world oriented 3-dimensional bin packing, which uses D-Wave's Leap Constrained Quadratic Model (CQM) Hybrid Solver.\n\nD-Wave's bin packing example demonstrates using a Leap hybrid CQM solver on constrained problems with binary variables, formulating the bin-packing problem as a constrained quadratic model.\n\n### Recent Manufacturing Facility Benchmark (2025)\n\nIn November 2025, D-Wave and BASF announced a joint proof-of-concept project using a hybrid-quantum application to optimize manufacturing workflows in a BASF liquid-filling facility, setting a new benchmark for manufacturing efficiency by reducing production scheduling time from 10 hours to just seconds.\n\nThe hybrid-quantum application outperformed an existing optimization solution across key operational metrics, reducing lateness by 14 percent, reducing setup times by 9 percent, and shortening tank unloading durations by up to 18 percent.\n\n### Performance Research\n\nResearch findings indicate that D-Wave's hybrid solver is currently most advantageous for integer quadratic objective functions and shows potential for quadratic constraints.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4630ec40-5a8d-482d-a907-5b598ef409ad","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:23.575Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3600cab8-0d44-4140-9762-cfce25a4bef9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
